    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.02320v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        The advancement of computational psychology requires AI tools capable of deeply understanding counseling dialogues. Existing audio <span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> (AudioLLMs) often rely on single speech encoders pre-<span class="search-hit mathjax">trained</span> on general data, struggling to capture domain-specific features like com&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.02320v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.02320v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.02320v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        The advancement of computational psychology requires AI tools capable of deeply understanding counseling dialogues. Existing audio <span class="search-hit mathjax">language</span> <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> (AudioLLMs) often rely on single speech encoders pre-<span class="search-hit mathjax">trained</span> on general data, struggling to capture domain-specific features like complex emotions and professional techniques. To address this, we propose WEE-Therapy, a multi-task AudioLLM incorporating a Weak Encoder Ensemble (WEE) mechanism. This supplements a powerful base encoder with a pool of lightweight, specialized encoders. A novel dual-routing strategy combines stable, data-independent domain knowledge with dynamic, data-dependent expert selection. Evaluated on emotion recognition, technique classification, risk detection, and summarization, WEE-Therapy achieves significant performance gains across all tasks with minimal parameter overhead, demonstrating strong potential for AI-assisted clinical analysis.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.02320v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.02320v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

